    rdfs:comment 'Reference data defining all health, retirement, and ancillary benefit plans offered to employees, with eligibility rules and provider details.' .

ind:BenefitEnrollment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Hr ;
    rdfs:label 'Benefit Enrollment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of employee enrollments, changes, and terminations for each benefit plan, capturing effective dates and coverage levels.' .

ind:TrainingCourse rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Hr ;
    rdfs:label 'Training Course' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference list of all training courses, certifications, and learning modules available to NCDOT staff, including delivery method and credit hours.' .

ind:TrainingRecord rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Hr ;
    rdfs:label 'Training Record' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of employee participation in training courses, capturing completion dates, scores, and certifications earned.' .

ind:LeaveRequest rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Hr ;
    rdfs:label 'Leave Request' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of employee leave applications, approvals, and usage, including leave type, start/end dates, and remaining balances.' .

ind:RecruitmentCandidate rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Hr ;
    rdfs:label 'Recruitment Candidate' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of external candidates applying for NCDOT positions, capturing resume data, interview stages, and hiring decisions.' .

ind:JobOpening rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Hr ;
    rdfs:label 'Job Opening' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of open positions, posting dates, requisition details, and fill status for internal and external hiring processes.' .

ind:SalaryGrade rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Hr ;
    rdfs:label 'Salary Grade' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference data defining salary grades, pay ranges, and associated position levels used for compensation planning.' .

ind:PerformanceReview rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Hr ;
    rdfs:label 'Performance Review' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of employee performance evaluations, including rating scores, reviewer comments, and development plans.' .

ind:TimeEntry rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Hr ;
    rdfs:label 'Time Entry' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Transactional record of daily employee work hours, project codes, and overtime, used for payroll and labor reporting.' .

ind:Skill rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Hr ;
    rdfs:label 'Skill' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference list of skill definitions and competency levels used for workforce planning and training alignment.' .

ind:Certification rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Hr ;
    rdfs:label 'Certification' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Reference data for professional certifications, licensing bodies, and renewal requirements relevant to NCDOT staff.' .

ind:Equipment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Asset ;
    rdfs:label 'Equipment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Consolidated equipment from highway and maintenance domains. Original: Master list of equipment and tools used in highway construction and maintenance, including type, cap... Also includes: Master inventory of maintenance equipment (e.g., snowplows, sweepers, rollers) with asset identifier...' .

ind:Incident rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Safety ;
    rdfs:label 'Incident' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Consolidated incident from aviation and rail domains. Original: Reported aviation incidents and accidents occurring at or near NCDOT airports, with investigation ou... Also includes: Documented rail incidents and accidents, with details on date, location, involved equipment, cause c... Also consolid Also consolidates: aviation.incident_report, environmental.environmental_incident.' .

ind:ProjectBudget rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Project ;
    rdfs:label 'Project Budget' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Consolidated budget from highway and project domains. Original: Budgetary allocations for highway projects, detailing funding source, amount, fiscal year, cost cate... Also includes: Master budget record for a project, detailing approved cost categories, allocated amounts, fiscal ye...' .

ind:FundingAllocation rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Funding Allocation' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Consolidated funding_allocation from planning and finance domains. Original: Details of how funding is allocated to projects or programs, including allocation amount, source (fe... Also includes: Transactional record of each grant allocation, linking funds to cost centers, projects, and reportin...' .

ind:Payment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Payment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Consolidated payment from dmv and procurement domains. Original: Transactional record of payments made to the DMV, linking to driver, vehicle, fee, payment method, a... Also includes: Payment record representing settlement of invoices, including payer, payee, amount, currency, paymen...' .

ind:Event rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Maintenance ;
    rdfs:label 'Event' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Consolidated event from ferry and maintenance domains. Original: Record of maintenance events performed on vessels, including type of work, date, service provider, a... Also includes: Transactional record of each maintenance activity performed, capturing actual labor hours, material ...' .

ind:SafetyInspection rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Safety ;
    rdfs:label 'Safety Inspection' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Consolidated inspection from aviation and safety domains. Original: Records of routine safety inspections performed on airports, runways, and navigation aids.... Also includes: Field inspections of roadway safety features (signage, guardrails, lighting, pavement markings) docu... Also consolidates: rail.track_inspection, safety.field_inspection.' .

ind:Agency rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Procurement ;
    rdfs:label 'Agency' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Consolidated agency from environmental and transit domains. Original: Reference list of external agencies (EPA, USACE, NCDEQ, FHWA, etc.) involved in environmental compli... Also includes: Master entity representing the operating agency or authority, with legal name, jurisdiction, funding...' .

ind:RouteStopSchedule rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Transit ;
    rdfs:label 'Route Stop Schedule' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the scheduled service relationship between transit routes and stops. It captures the operational schedule defining which stops are served by which routes, in what sequence, and at what times. Each record links one route to one stop with scheduling attributes that exist only in the context of this specific route-stop pairing. This is the foundational data structure for trip planning, schedule adherence monitoring, and service coverage analysis.. Existence Justification: In transit operations, routes serve multiple stops and stops are served by multiple routes. This is the fundamental operational relationship in public transportation, explicitly managed through schedule planning processes. Transit planners actively create, update, and delete route-stop assignments during service planning cycles, and each assignment carries critical scheduling data (sequence, arrival/departure times, pickup/drop-off rules) that belongs to neither the route nor the stop alone.' .

ind:PavementTreatment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Highway ;
    rdfs:label 'Pavement Treatment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the treatment event between pavement_section and project. It captures the specific work performed on a pavement section as part of a transportation project. Each record links one pavement_section to one project with attributes that describe the treatment type, timing, scope, and condition assessment before and after the work.. Existence Justification: In NCDOT pavement management operations, a single pavement section receives multiple treatments over its lifecycle (crack seal in 2020, overlay in 2023, rehabilitation in 2028), and a single transportation project typically treats multiple pavement sections (a district-wide resurfacing contract may treat 50+ sections). The relationship between pavement sections and projects is operationally managed as treatment events with specific attributes: treatment type, scheduled and actual dates, before/after condition ratings, and work scope details.' .

ind:ConstructionImpact rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Highway ;
    rdfs:label 'Construction Impact' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the impact event between construction_activity and route. It captures the specific effects of highway construction on transit route operations, including detours, service modifications, and public notification requirements. Each record links one construction_activity to one route with attributes that exist only in the context of this relationship.. Existence Justification: Highway construction activities frequently impact multiple transit routes simultaneously when work occurs in areas served by multiple bus, rail, or ferry routes. Conversely, each transit route is affected by multiple construction activities over time as different highway segments along or near the route undergo maintenance and improvement. NCDOT actively manages these impacts as operational events, tracking specific detour requirements, service modifications, and public notification status for each construction-route combination to coordinate multimodal transportation operations.' .

ind:CorridorSegment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Planning ;
    rdfs:label 'Corridor Segment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the membership relationship between highway segments and planning corridors. It captures the inclusion of specific highway segments within defined transportation corridors for planning, analysis, and phased improvement tracking. Each record links one segment to one corridor with attributes that define the segment\'s position and role within that corridor context.. Existence Justification: In NCDOT planning operations, highway segments are operational assets that can belong to multiple overlapping planning corridors simultaneously (e.g., a segment of US-1 may be part of the US-1 Strategic Corridor, the Triangle Regional Freight Corridor, and the Capital Area Mobility Corridor). Conversely, planning corridors are multi-segment constructs that span dozens to hundreds of segments for corridor-level analysis, STIP project development, and phased improvement planning. Planners actively manage these segment-corridor memberships, tracking each segment\'s position, role, and inclusion status within each corridor context.' .

ind:SegmentScenarioTreatment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Highway ;
    rdfs:label 'Segment Scenario Treatment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the treatment or improvement strategy applied to a specific highway segment within a specific planning scenario. It captures the investment decisions, cost estimates, and implementation priorities that exist only in the context of evaluating a segment under a particular planning scenario. Each record links one segment to one scenario with attributes describing the proposed treatment approach.. Existence Justification: In transportation planning operations, NCDOT creates multiple planning scenarios (baseline, growth, climate-impact) to evaluate different investment strategies. Each scenario evaluates hundreds or thousands of highway segments with different proposed treatments, costs, and priorities. A single segment appears in multiple scenarios with different treatment approaches (e.g., overlay in baseline, reconstruction in growth scenario), and each scenario includes many segments. Planning analysts actively manage these segment-scenario-treatment combinations to compare funding allocation strategies.' .

ind:ContractSegment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Procurement ;
    rdfs:label 'Contract Segment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the work scope assignment between highway segments and procurement contracts. It captures the specific work to be performed on each segment under each contract, including milepost boundaries, work scope details, status tracking, and completion progress. Each record links one segment to one contract with attributes that exist only in the context of this contractual work assignment.. Existence Justification: In NCDOT highway operations, a single procurement contract routinely covers work on multiple highway segments (e.g., a resurfacing contract for a 50-mile corridor spanning 20 distinct segments), and conversely, a single segment frequently has multiple active contracts simultaneously for different types of work (resurfacing, guardrail replacement, drainage improvements, bridge work). Highway maintenance and construction managers actively track work scope, progress, completion percentage, and status for each segment-contract combination as a distinct operational unit.' .

ind:Assignment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Maintenance ;
    rdfs:label 'Assignment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the operational assignment of maintenance crews to highway segments for specific maintenance work. It captures the work scheduling, crew deployment, and maintenance activity tracking that occurs when NCDOT assigns crews to perform maintenance on highway segments. Each record links one crew to one segment with attributes that exist only in the context of this specific work assignment.. Existence Justification: In NCDOT maintenance operations, crews are assigned to multiple highway segments over time for different maintenance activities (pothole repair, crack sealing, mowing, etc.), and each segment requires multiple crews throughout the year for various maintenance needs. The assignment itself is an operational business entity that maintenance supervisors actively create, schedule, track, and close out, with specific attributes like work type, assignment dates, duration, status, and costs that belong to the assignment relationship rather than to the crew or segment alone.' .

ind:MaterialApplication rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Maintenance ;
    rdfs:label 'Material Application' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Event of applying maintenance materials to pavement sections. It captures the operational record of material usage during maintenance, resurfacing, or rehabilitation activities. Each record links one material to one pavement section with attributes that exist only in the context of this specific application event.. Existence Justification: In NCDOT maintenance operations, materials (asphalt, sealant, concrete, etc.) are applied to multiple pavement sections across the highway network, and each pavement section receives multiple different materials over its lifecycle during routine maintenance, resurfacing, and rehabilitation activities. The business actively manages and tracks each material application as an operational event with specific quantities, dates, methods, costs, and work order references.' .

ind:CrashInvolvement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Dmv ;
    rdfs:label 'Crash Involvement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the involvement of a driver in a crash event. It captures the specific role, fault determination, injury status, and citations for each driver involved in each crash. Each record links one driver to one crash_report with attributes that exist only in the context of this specific involvement.. Existence Justification: In NCDOT operations, a single crash event routinely involves multiple drivers (multi-vehicle collisions, witnesses, pedestrians), and individual drivers accumulate involvement in multiple crashes over their driving history. Law enforcement and safety investigators actively manage crash involvement records as operational entities, documenting each driver\'s specific role, fault determination, injury status, and citations issued at the scene. This is not an analytical correlation but an operational business process where crash investigators create, update, and query involvement records.' .

ind:VehicleCrashInvolvement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Dmv ;
    rdfs:label 'Vehicle Crash Involvement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the involvement of a specific vehicle in a specific crash event. It captures the operational details of each vehicle\'s participation in a crash, including the vehicle\'s role in the collision, damage assessment, towing status, and occupant count. Each record links one vehicle to one crash report with attributes that exist only in the context of this specific involvement.. Existence Justification: In North Carolina crash reporting operations, a single crash event routinely involves multiple vehicles (pile-ups, intersection collisions, multi-vehicle chain reactions), and any given vehicle can be involved in multiple separate crash events over its registration lifetime. NCDOT crash investigators actively create and manage vehicle involvement records as part of the crash investigation process, documenting each vehicle\'s specific role, damage level, and contributing factors for every crash.' .

ind:StakeholderEngagement rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Project ;
    rdfs:label 'Stakeholder Engagement' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the formal engagement relationship between a transportation project and a stakeholder entity. It captures the stakeholder\'s role, engagement requirements, notification obligations, and approval authority for each specific project. Each record links one project to one stakeholder with attributes that exist only in the context of this project-stakeholder relationship.. Existence Justification: In NCDOT transportation project delivery, projects routinely engage multiple stakeholders (MPOs, RPOs, local governments, utilities, property owners, regulatory agencies, community groups), and each stakeholder entity participates in multiple projects across their jurisdiction or area of interest. Public involvement coordinators and project managers actively manage these engagement relationships, tracking each stakeholder\'s specific role, required engagement level, notification obligations, and approval authority on a per-project basis for regulatory compliance (NEPA, SEPA, federal aid requirements) and coordination purposes.' .

ind:TrackInspection rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Rail ;
    rdfs:label 'Track Inspection' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Event of a safety inspection being performed on a specific track segment. It captures the inspection findings, compliance status, and defects identified for each track segment during each inspection. Each record links one track segment to one safety inspection with attributes that exist only in the context of this specific inspection-segment relationship.. Existence Justification: In rail operations, track segments undergo multiple safety inspections over time (geometry checks, rail condition assessments, tie inspections), and each safety inspection event typically covers multiple contiguous track segments along a line or subdivision. The business actively manages inspection-segment pairings as operational records, tracking specific findings, compliance status, and defect counts for each segment during each inspection. This is a true operational M:N relationship where the inspection-segment pairing carries meaningful data.' .

ind:ProgramVendorEligibility rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Grant ;
    rdfs:label 'Program Vendor Eligibility' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the prequalification and eligibility relationship between grant programs and vendors. It captures program-specific vendor certifications, eligibility status, and qualification dates that exist only in the context of a specific program-vendor combination. Each record links one grant program to one vendor with attributes tracking their eligibility and certification status for that specific program.. Existence Justification: In NCDOT grant administration, vendors must be prequalified for specific grant programs based on program-specific eligibility criteria and certifications. A single vendor can be eligible for multiple grant programs (e.g., a DBE-certified vendor may be prequalified for multiple federal highway programs), and each grant program maintains a roster of multiple eligible vendors. The eligibility relationship itself carries program-specific data including prequalification dates, certification types, eligibility status, and expiration dates that belong to neither the vendor master record nor the program master record alone.' .

ind:ContractAssignment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Procurement ;
    rdfs:label 'Contract Assignment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the assignment relationship between contracts and employees at NCDOT. It captures the formal assignment of NCDOT employees to contracts in specific roles (contract manager, technical lead, financial officer, compliance officer) with defined responsibilities and accountability. Each record links one contract to one employee with attributes that exist only in the context of this assignment relationship.. Existence Justification: In NCDOT operations, large contracts (construction, consulting, professional services) require multiple employees to be assigned in different roles such as contract manager, technical lead, financial officer, compliance officer, and inspectors. Each employee can be assigned to multiple contracts simultaneously with varying responsibility percentages. The business actively manages these assignments to track accountability, workload distribution, and ensure proper oversight of contract execution.' .

ind:ProjectAssignment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Hr ;
    rdfs:label 'Project Assignment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the Assignment between employee and project_boundary. It captures the formal assignment of NCDOT employees to transportation projects with specific roles, responsibilities, and time periods. Each record links one employee to one project boundary with attributes that exist only in the context of this assignment relationship.. Existence Justification: In NCDOT operations, transportation projects require multiple employees with different roles (project managers, engineers, inspectors, environmental specialists, ROW agents) working simultaneously or sequentially on the same project. Conversely, employees work on multiple projects across different districts and time periods throughout their careers. The business actively manages these assignments with specific roles, responsibility areas, and time periods for resource allocation, project staffing, and workforce utilization tracking.' .

ind:CrewAssignment rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Maintenance ;
    rdfs:label 'Crew Assignment' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Assignment of maintenance crews to work orders or construction activities, capturing crew composition, skill sets, shift timing, and work completion status. This association product represents the operational reality that multiple crews can be assigned to a single work order (e.g., electrical, structural, paving crews working on the same bridge repair), and crews are assigned to many work orders over time. Each record links crew members to specific work assignments including highway maintenance, construction projects, ferry sailing operations, and emergency response activities. Tracks crew role, hours worked, assignment timing, completion status, labor costs, materials used, safety compliance, and quality inspection results. Originally consolidated from highway and ferry domains, now unified with maintenance operations to serve as the single source of truth for all crew assignment tracking across NCDOT.' .

ind:InspectionRecord rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Bridge ;
    rdfs:label 'Inspection Record' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This product represents the comprehensive record of bridge inspection events, capturing the execution of specific inspection types on bridges throughout the NCDOT inventory. Each record documents when an inspection occurred, who performed it, detailed condition ratings across all bridge components (deck, superstructure, substructure, channel, culvert), observed defects and their severity, recommended actions, and when the next inspection is due. In NCDOT bridge asset management operations, each bridge undergoes multiple types of inspections throughout its lifecycle (routine, fracture-critical, underwater, special, post-event), with each inspection event carrying specific data about findings, structural evaluations, load ratings, scour conditions, and compliance with National Bridge Inspection Standards (NBIS). This product serves as the single source of truth for all bridge inspection findings, condition assessments, and recommended maintenance actions.' .

ind:ProjectFunding rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Finance ;
    rdfs:label 'Project Funding' ;
    rdfs:comment 'This association product represents the allocation of funding sources to transportation projects. It captures the financial commitment of specific funding allocations to project scopes, tracking the amount, timing, fiscal year, phase, status, and percentage of each fund-to-project relationship. Each record links one funding source to one project with attributes that exist only in the context of this funding relationship. In NCDOT operations, transportation projects routinely receive funding from multiple sources (federal STIP allocations, HSIP grants, state bonds, local matching funds, CMAQ programs, special revenue funds), and each funding source typically supports multiple projects across the state. The finance and planning teams actively manage these fund-to-project allocations through the STIP (State Transportation Improvement Program) process, tracking specific amounts, fiscal years, allocation dates, project phases (preliminary engineering, right-of-way, construction), statuses (planned, committed, obligated, expended), expenditure amounts, and percentage splits for compliance reporting to federal agencies and state oversight bodies.' .

ind:Funding rdf:type rdfs:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf ind:Project ;
    rdfs:label 'Funding' ;
    rdfs:comment 'Consolidated funding from bridge and project domains. Original: Master record of funding allocations for bridge projects, capturing source (federal, state, grant), ... Also includes: Master data for external funding sources (e.g., FHWA, FTA, BUILD) linked to projects, including gran...' .

